  <prompt>Scaffold a NEW .NET 10 (TFM net10.0) project at src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane/ with: (a) Program.cs using minimal API + WebApplication builder; (b) Startup module composition (extension methods per feature area to avoid god-class DI); (c) JWT Bearer authentication with audience api://spaarke-provisioning-controlplane-{env}; (d) Operator + Reader app-role authorization policies; (e) OpenAPI/Swashbuckle at /swagger. Include a Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.csproj (net10.0, TreatWarningsAsErrors=true, nullable enable) + a top-level SolutionInclusion.md OR update spaarke.sln to include the new project.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer with .NET 10 minimal API + JWT Bearer + app-role authorization + Swashbuckle expertise. Follow ADR-010 DI minimalism: L2 has its own DI graph independent of BFF; do NOT reference BFF assemblies from L2.</role>
  <goal>src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane/ project exists as a valid net10.0 minimal API scaffold: Program.cs boots WebApplication with JWT auth + Operator/Reader policies + Swagger at /swagger; dotnet build exits 0 with 0 errors + 0 warnings (analyzers-as-errors); a placeholder /ping endpoint returns 200 (unauthenticated) and a placeholder /api/runs POST endpoint returns 401 without bearer token.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Spec FR-20 + design.md §5.2 (L2 in dedicated service, NOT BFF) + spec.md § New Components row 1: L2 control-plane is a new .NET 10 App Service in rg-spaarke-platform-{env}. It sequences all 19 handlers, exposes REST + AAD, and hosts the state-reconciler BackgroundService. Every provisioning run flows through this project. Without the scaffold, no handler infrastructure can register; every downstream Wave C3/C4/C5 task is blocked.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="new">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.csproj</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane/Program.cs</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane/Modules/AuthModule.cs</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane/Modules/SwaggerModule.cs</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane/Endpoints/HealthEndpoints.cs</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane/appsettings.json</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Program.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/</file>
      <file role="modify">spaarke.sln</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="none" status="complete">No prerequisite r1 task — Wave C3 kickoff. Task 024 authored the POCO Models subfolder; this task scaffolds the .csproj that compiles it.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-010">Scope: L2 has its own DI graph. Do NOT reference BFF (Sprk.Bff.Api) assemblies from L2 — L2 reuses infrastructure PATTERNS (via canonical reference reading), not compiled dependencies. Register services via module extension methods (parity with BFF's *Module.cs pattern) to avoid god-class DI.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">Scope: JWT Bearer configuration uses UAMI identity for downstream calls (KV, Cosmos data-plane, Service Bus). Audience api://spaarke-provisioning-controlplane-{env}; issuer https://sts.windows.net/{spaarkeTenantId}/.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-032">Scope: any conditional service registered in L2 must follow the Null-Object kill-switch pattern P1/P2/P3 (per §10 §F.1 anti-pattern rule) — do NOT emit if (flag) { AddService } blocks without a Null-Object counterpart.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">FR-20 acceptance: L3 skill can auth via az account get-access-token; Operator-role required for mutating endpoints returns 403 without role. This task scaffolds the authorization policies; downstream tasks add the mutating endpoints.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">MUST use .NET 10 (TFM net10.0), Directory.Build.props inheritance (TreatWarningsAsErrors=true + analyzers-as-errors per NFR-06), and nullable reference types enabled.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">MUST NOT touch src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/** — L2 is a peer service, not a BFF extension.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope (this task only): scaffold + placeholder /ping + placeholder /api/runs POST that returns 401 unauth. Do NOT wire Cosmos, Service Bus, or App Insights (those are tasks 037/038/039).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Publish-size impact: L2 is a SEPARATE App Service; its publish size is NOT part of the BFF ≤60 MB ceiling (NFR-01 scopes to BFF). Report L2's own publish size baseline in task notes for future L2-scope tracking.</constraint>
  </constraints>

