    <patterns>
      <pattern name="BFF Program.cs minimal API bootstrap" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Program.cs">Mirror the WebApplication builder + module composition pattern (AddAuthentication, AddAuthorization, module extension methods).</pattern>
      <pattern name="BFF *Module.cs DI pattern" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/">Extension-method-per-module registration to avoid god-class Program.cs (respect NFR-07 god-class ratchet).</pattern>
      <pattern name="Endpoint filter pattern (Registration endpoints)" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Registration/">Mirror the endpoint-filter registration for authorization enforcement.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="prescriptive">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Output the RIGOR LEVEL declaration (FULL + reason — l2-controlplane + auth + NEW surface). Load spec.md FR-20, design.md §5.2, ADR-010, ADR-028, ADR-032, ADR-036.</step>
    <step order="1">Create the folder src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane/ and initialize a net10.0 minimal API .csproj (dotnet new webapi -f net10.0, then adjust per Directory.Build.props inheritance).</step>
    <step order="2">Add PackageReferences: Microsoft.AspNetCore.Authentication.JwtBearer, Microsoft.Identity.Web (or Microsoft.AspNetCore.Authorization), Swashbuckle.AspNetCore, Microsoft.ApplicationInsights.AspNetCore (deferred wiring to task 039 but reference now), Azure.Identity, System.Text.Json. Verify zero HIGH-severity CVEs per NFR-02.</step>
    <step order="3">Author Program.cs with WebApplication.CreateBuilder pattern + module composition (AddAuthModule, AddSwaggerModule, MapHealthEndpoints).</step>
    <step order="4">Author Modules/AuthModule.cs: AddAuthentication().AddJwtBearer(...) with audience api://spaarke-provisioning-controlplane-{env}; AddAuthorization with policies Operator (requires app-role Operator) + Reader (requires app-role Reader OR Operator).</step>
    <step order="5">Author Modules/SwaggerModule.cs: Swashbuckle at /swagger with bearer-token security scheme.</step>
    <step order="6">Author Endpoints/HealthEndpoints.cs: MapGet("/ping") returning "ok" (AllowAnonymous); MapPost("/api/runs") returning Results.StatusCode(501) — placeholder — under RequireAuthorization("Operator").</step>
    <step order="7">Add src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane/ project to spaarke.sln.</step>
    <step order="8">Run dotnet build src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane/ -c Release — verify 0 errors, 0 warnings (analyzers-as-errors).</step>
    <step order="9">Run dotnet publish -c Release -o deploy/l2-publish/ — record baseline publish size in task notes (this is L2's own ceiling; NOT counted against BFF NFR-01).</step>
    <step order="10">Update TASK-INDEX.md: set this task's status to ✅.</step>
    <step order="11">Document deviation (e.g. Microsoft.Identity.Web vs raw JwtBearer choice, folder structure nuance) in projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If DI registration for the placeholder /api/runs endpoint collides with a BFF-namespace type OR the Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane project accidentally references Sprk.Bff.Api compiled output, STOP and escalate per CLAUDE.md §6 — L2 must be a peer, not a dependency-referrer.</trigger>
    <trigger>If Microsoft.AspNetCore.Authentication.JwtBearer or Microsoft.Identity.Web has a HIGH-severity CVE (dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive), STOP and escalate — do NOT add a package with an open HIGH CVE per NFR-02.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>None. src/server/services/ does not exist (verified via ls); Sprk.Bff.Api is per-customer, not fleet-scoped. spec.md § New Components row 1 documents this explicitly: "L2 control-plane .NET 10 App Service — no existing overlap."</existing>
    <extension>No — BFF's per-customer nature + ADR-010 DI minimalism + §10 BFF Hygiene binding-rule preclude adding fleet orchestration to BFF. L2 is a distinct project.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Without L2 scaffold, provisioning stays 3-generation fragmented (13 known issues per ENV-GUIDE per spec.md § New Components row 1); no unified state; operator manually merges 3 docs per §2; every downstream Wave C4 handler task blocked. Every Phase D/F acceptance criterion cascades to failure.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

