  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given dotnet build src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane/ -c Release, exit is 0 with 0 errors + 0 warnings (analyzers-as-errors).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given dotnet run on the scaffold, GET /ping returns 200 with body "ok" (unauthenticated); GET /swagger returns 200.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given POST /api/runs without an Authorization header, response is 401 Unauthorized.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a valid bearer token with app-role Operator, POST /api/runs returns 501 (placeholder — will be implemented in Wave C5).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a valid bearer token WITHOUT app-role Operator, POST /api/runs returns 403 Forbidden.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive, 0 HIGH-severity CVEs.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: no reference to Sprk.Bff.Api project OR its compiled DLLs; L2 is a peer.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: no Cosmos, Service Bus, or App Insights wiring in this task (deferred to 037/038/039).</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Maps spec.md FR-20 + § New Components row 1 acceptance. The placeholder endpoints validate the auth + routing wiring without committing to handler implementations. Tasks 037/038/039 add Cosmos client + Service Bus client + App Insights wiring on top of this scaffold. L2's publish size is L2's own ceiling; NOT part of BFF NFR-01 60 MB budget.</notes>

